            <ArticleTitle>A new syndrome: right-sided arcus aorta syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2013-009569</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2013009569</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Right-sided arcus aorta (RSAA) is a rare congenital anomaly that may cause chronic cough and dyspnoea. We aimed to define RSAA as a new syndrome characterised by RSAA, dyspnoea and cough during exercise. RSAA syndrome should be included in the differential diagnosis of asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
